    description: "DEEP bakeoff (deep-20260409-054615) found all 13 tier2-only nodes in alertmanager are _test.go files or test utilities (mock.go, acceptance.go). Root cause: detect_package_roots() in supply_chain.py (lines 541-623) only handles npm/Cargo/Maven workspaces — Go modules (go.mod) are never detected. Without workspace detection, the generic test pattern check (lines 451-466) demotes ALL _test.go files to tier-2 (INTERNAL_DEP). Fix: add Go module detection to detect_package_roots() so that go.mod presence registers the repo root as a package root, allowing the workspace-aware tier logic (lines 421-449) to correctly classify co-located test files as tier-1. This is a root-cause fix, not a workaround. Structural scope expansion: check if Rust (Cargo.toml without workspace), Python (pyproject.toml without workspace), and other single-package layouts have the same bug."  # ca0f
    fields: {}  # ca0f
